bug_report:
musttail gives bogus volatile function error message
Consider the example:

[[noreturn]] void abort_like() noexcept;
void just_void() noexcept;

void test1() { abort_like(); }
void test2() { just_void(); }


Calling a function without `[[noreturn]]` results in just a `jmp`. Function with `[[noreturn]]` additionally touches `rsp` and uses `call`:

"test1()":
        sub     rsp, 8
        call    "abort_like()"
"test2()":
        jmp     "just_void()"


Godbolt playground:https://godbolt.org/z/6xfn76e81
